# Boethius: servants and other goods counted as possessions are not really one's own
atom	servants_vicious	the servants behave viciously
atom	servants_burden	the servants are a ruinous burden to thy house and dangerous to their master
atom	servants_honest	the servants are honest
atom	virtue_others	the servants' goodness is other men's virtue
atom	servants_thine	the servants (their worth) can be counted in the sum of thy possessions
atom	possessions_thine	the things thou reckonest among thy possessions are really thine
atom	beautiful	these things are beautiful in their own nature
atom	beauty_thine	their beauty is anything to thee
atom	ground_grief_joy	thou hast reason to grieve for their loss or find joy in their possession
atom	pleasing_without	they would have been no less pleasing in themselves though never included among thy possessions
atom	precious_from_counting	they derive their preciousness from being counted in thy riches
